      "impact": "The EPD panel's VDD/VDDIO (Display_Power_Switch) rail is decoupled with 10x less capacitance than the reference circuit intends, so the display supply sees more ripple and the boost/charge-pump stage has a weaker local reservoir.",
      "confidence": 0.5
    },
    {
      "category": "missing_component",
      "components": ["C12"],
      "pins": ["IC1.A2", "IC1.B2"],
      "nets": ["BAT+"],
      "observed": "The EthernetAndPower sheet contains only C11 (0.1 uF, at the RJ45) and C13 (10 uF, at the +3V3 output); no C12 symbol exists anywhere on the BAT+ rail feeding IC1.",
      "expected": "A 2.2 uF input capacitor (C12) from BAT+ to GND at the FAN53610 VIN, as required by the spec and by the FAN53610 datasheet's recommended CIN.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "`C12` (2.2 µF) on `BAT+`→GND is the input cap; `C13` (10 µF) on `+3V3`→GND is the output cap"}
      ],
      "impact": "The buck regulator has no local input capacitance on BAT+, giving poor input decoupling / higher input ripple and possible instability when the switching load steps, contrary to the intended design.",
      "confidence": 0.4
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The build deviates from the specified reference in the analog/power sections: the EPD rail decoupling cap C1 is drawn as 0.1 uF/16 V instead of the specified 1 uF/25 V, and the FAN53610's specified 2.2 uF input capacitor C12 is absent from the BAT+ rail. Both are direct contradictions of explicit statements in the design specification, so an anomaly is reported, though overall confidence is only moderate because these were read from a rendered schematic."
}

